      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 6.19,
      "end_seconds": 11.24,
      "duration_seconds": 5.05,
      "text": "Yes, come in and sit down. What brings you here today?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 12.97,
      "end_seconds": 18.62,
      "duration_seconds": 5.65,
      "text": "doctor, I'll sit in if that's okay, I know what's been happening"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 20.29,
      "end_seconds": 23.47,
      "duration_seconds": 3.18,
      "text": "Please do. Extra information is always welcome."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 25.14,
      "end_seconds": 33.24,
      "duration_seconds": 8.1,
      "text": "mainly vomiting blood there's a couple of other things, um, but that's the main one"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 34.69,
      "end_seconds": 36.62,
      "duration_seconds": 1.93,
      "text": "When did this begin?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 38.54,
      "end_seconds": 41.51,
      "duration_seconds": 2.97,
      "text": "I've had it for six months."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 42.28,
      "end_seconds": 44.89,
      "duration_seconds": 2.61,
      "text": "How often do you get it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 46.94,
      "end_seconds": 69.91,
      "duration_seconds": 22.97,
      "text": "It happens every other day. And stomach pain, too. Um, about stomach pain, I'd say moderate. Yeah, I've been feeling faint too. Uh, with feeling faint, I'd say severe. Honestly, every other day. It's worse with standing. It It settles a little with lying down."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 71.51,
      "end_seconds": 74.3,
      "duration_seconds": 2.79,
      "text": "Any chest pain or fever at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 76.16,
      "end_seconds": 79.55,
      "duration_seconds": 3.39,
      "text": "No, I haven't had any of them."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 81.16,
      "end_seconds": 85.36,
      "duration_seconds": 4.2,
      "text": "Anything with your heart, like skipped beats or fainting?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 87.25,
      "end_seconds": 89.35,
      "duration_seconds": 2.1,
      "text": "nothing like that that"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 91.33,
      "end_seconds": 94.63,
      "duration_seconds": 3.3,
      "text": "How are your joints, any aches elsewhere?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 96.35,
      "end_seconds": 97.94,
      "duration_seconds": 1.59,
      "text": "No, nothing there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 115.07,
      "end_seconds": 120.46,
      "duration_seconds": 5.39,
      "text": "Okay, tell me about your routine, work, habits, that sort of thing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 121.29,
      "end_seconds": 130.82,
      "duration_seconds": 9.53,
      "text": "I'm a hairdresser, on my feet all day. I swim twice a week. Lots of rice, lentils and some fruit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 144.68,
      "end_seconds": 147.91,
      "duration_seconds": 3.23,
      "text": "Do you take any prescribed or over-the-counter medicines?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 148.51,
      "end_seconds": 154.23,
      "duration_seconds": 5.72,
      "text": "well, she takes escitalopram, 10 milligrams, once a day for the anxiety"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 169.16,
      "end_seconds": 174.17,
      "duration_seconds": 5.01,
      "text": "So, tell me about any past illnesses or ongoing conditions."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 175.78,
      "end_seconds": 178.5,
      "duration_seconds": 2.72,
      "text": "Anxiety, for nearly five years"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 179.3,
      "end_seconds": 183.89,
      "duration_seconds": 4.59,
      "text": "So, can I check a few measurements before we carry on?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 191.22,
      "end_seconds": 193.78,
      "duration_seconds": 2.56,
      "text": "Okay, this won't take long..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 214.9,
      "end_seconds": 222.33,
      "duration_seconds": 7.43,
      "text": "Okay: BP is 121 over 73, heart rate 122, temperature 36.7, SpO2 98 percent on room air."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 224.89,
      "end_seconds": 226.87,
      "duration_seconds": 1.98,
      "text": "May I examine you now?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 227.75,
      "end_seconds": 229.86,
      "duration_seconds": 2.11,
      "text": "Raise your arm for me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 237.41,
      "end_seconds": 244.02,
      "duration_seconds": 6.61,
      "text": "You look pale, your pulse is fast and your tummy is tender at the top."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 248.39,
      "end_seconds": 266.27,
      "duration_seconds": 17.88,
      "text": "okay, that's enough for me right, here's what I'm thinking it fits best with a possible bleeding stomach ulcer that's my thinking for now, and it may change as we learn more we shouldn't forget a bleed from the gullet"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 266.88,
      "end_seconds": 270.5,
      "duration_seconds": 3.62,
      "text": "um, do you think it's something serious?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 272.26,
      "end_seconds": 304.57,
      "duration_seconds": 32.31,
      "text": "I can't promise yet, but most people with a possible bleeding stomach ulcer do well once it's treated properly. We should do an endoscopy for bleeding. Let's book urgent blood tests to look into bleeding. Please stop the ibuprofen and do not eat or drink. A short walk every day, even twenty minutes, will help more than you'd think. The emergency team would be the right next step, I'll refer you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 305.56,
      "end_seconds": 307.92,
      "duration_seconds": 2.36,
      "text": "sure, where do I go?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 309.25,
      "end_seconds": 315.2,
      "duration_seconds": 5.95,
      "text": "Book a review straight away. That's everything on my side. Anything you're unsure about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 316.9,
      "end_seconds": 319.98,
      "duration_seconds": 3.08,
      "text": "Great, thank you for your help."
    }
  ]
}